    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23222" root="شهل" body-key="$">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهِلَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهَلَ</span></b> , (K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهَلٌ</span>, (S, * O, * TA,)
<i>He</i> (a man, S, O) <i>had that quality of the eye
which is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُهْلَةٌ</span> [expl. below]; (S, O, K;)
as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اشهلّ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِشْهِلَالٌ</span>. (K.) [And in like
manner each of these verbs is probably used as
said of the eye.]

